{{ analysis_json }}

This is a partial-release recovery audit. The deterministic part of the
harness has already:

- Recreated local branch `{{ release_branch }}` on a fresh snapshot of
  `{{ base_branch }}` without moving any prior immutable remote attempt.
- Injected the recovered `## v{{ target_version }}` body verbatim above
  the next-older version heading.
- **Preserved `## Unreleased` as-is** — its entries describe work
  that landed after the original pin and is not part of the recovered
  release content. Those entries belong in the next release.
- Preserved an existing `{{ fixup_tag }}` exactly when present. If the tag is
  absent, the later ship stage will create it at the exact publication OID.

Do one bounded evidence pass:

- `release_read CHANGELOG.md` — see both the v{{ target_version }}
  section and `## Unreleased`. If `{{ fixup_tag }}` exists, confirm
  v{{ target_version }} matches it; in either state, confirm nothing in
  Unreleased obviously belongs inside v{{ target_version }}.
- `release_run` with
  `git log --oneline {{ recovery_oid }}..origin/{{ base_branch }}` — see what
  landed on `{{ base_branch }}` after the immutable recovery commit so you can
  spot misclassified Unreleased entries.
- `release_search` on one representative Unreleased entry to confirm
  it is not part of the recovered release content.

Return one short Audit block when finalization arrives. Do not produce a draft
changelog. If you find an Unreleased entry that should be in
v{{ target_version }}, flag it for the operator before the PR merges.
